/* German. Two conventions worth stating because they are easy to get wrong
   and invisible once wrong:

   - Duzen throughout, and mostly avoided: German UI reads better as a noun
     phrase than as an instruction ("Postfach wählen", not "Wähle ein
     Postfach"). Apple's own German follows the same rule.
   - "E-Mail" keeps its hyphen and stays feminine. "Mail" alone is common in
     speech but looks like an English leftover in an interface. */

